Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:22:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/24] Test checkpoint barriers under the durability decisions

CheckpointDurability_Tests: the degraded commit these tests started from
exists only without durable commits now. The recovery-marker and failed
checkpoint-sync tests run in both modes (a durable commit survives power
loss; an opted-out one only behind a synced barrier) and assert that the
failed checkpoint keeps reads exact, records the failure and refuses the
next write instead of closing the engine (decision 6). The "cannot sync"
checkpoint and retry tests run without durable commits (default A); a new
durable test asserts the commit on such a log fails with an unknown
outcome, keeps reading, and leaves process-crash and power-loss images
that recover to exactly the new and old states.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
